#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-Debugging.rst:12
msgid ""
"Sometimes your robot won't behave as you expected. This article summarizes "
"the ROS developer tools and guidance available to help with debugging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-Debugging.rst:30
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-Debugging.rst:33
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-Debugging.rst:35
msgid ""
"ROS provides a range of tools to help developers build, test, and monitor "
"robotic systems. Debugging is an essential part of development, and many of "
"these tools can be used to identify and fix issues. Some of the tools are "
"also useful for other aspects of robotic system development. For example, "
"debugging overlaps with introspection, analysis, node management, "
"visualization, and simulation, as these activities are often used to "
"investigate and diagnose issues in a system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-Debugging.rst:41
msgid "Core ROS packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-Debugging.rst:43
msgid ""
"`ros2doctor <https://docs.ros.org/en/rolling/p/ros2doctor/>`__: Command-line "
"tool to check for common misconfigurations in a ROS system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-Debugging.rst:45
msgid ""
"`tracetools <https://docs.ros.org/en/rolling/p/tracetools/>`__: Trace points "
"for creating and debugging execution traces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-Debugging.rst:47
msgid ""
"`rosbag2 <https://docs.ros.org/en/rolling/p/rosbag2/>`__: Record and play "
"back data moving across topics, services, and actions in a ROS application, "
"for later visualization and debugging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-Debugging.rst:49
msgid ""
"`ros2cli <https://github.com/ros2/ros2cli>`__: ROS command-line tools for "
"debugging, such as ``ros2 action``, ``ros2 node``, ``ros2 param``, ``ros2 "
"pkg``, and ``ros2 service``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-Debugging.rst:51
msgid ""
"`rviz <https://github.com/ros2/rviz>`__ and `rviz default plugins <https://"
"github.com/ros2/rviz/tree/rolling/rviz_default_plugins>`__: 3D robot "
"visualization tool for the ROS framework."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-Debugging.rst:53
msgid ""
"`rqt_gui and dependent packages <https://index.ros.org/p/rqt_gui/#rolling-"
"deps>`__: Tool for starting an instance of the ROS integrated graphical user "
"interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-Debugging.rst:56
msgid "Community-contributed packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-Debugging.rst:58
msgid ""
"`PlotJuggler <https://docs.ros.org/en/rolling/p/plotjuggler/>`__: A tool for "
"visualizing and analyzing data from ROS applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-Debugging.rst:60
msgid ""
"`Foxglove <https://foxglove.dev/>`__: A collection of tools for visualizing "
"and debugging robot data throughout the development lifecycle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/About-Debugging.rst:62
msgid ""
"`Rerun <https://github.com/rerun-io/rerun>`__: Tool to visualize, query, and "
"debug data from robotics, computer vision, and physical AI systems."
msgstr ""
